# 📌 About

This guide explains how to install and run Linux inside Termux using `proot-distro`.

This method runs Linux in CLI mode (Terminal only) without GUI.

Perfect for:
- Programming
- Python Development
- Linux Learning
- Termux Tools
- Lightweight Usage

---

# ⚡ Update Termux

```bash
pkg update && pkg upgrade -y
```

---

# 📦 Install proot-distro

```bash
pkg install proot-distro -y
```

---

# 📜 Show Available Linux Distributions

```bash
proot-distro list
```

---

# 🐧 Install Ubuntu

```bash
proot-distro install ubuntu
```

---

# 🚀 Start Linux

```bash
proot-distro login ubuntu
```

If Linux starts successfully, you will see something like:

```bash
root@localhost:~#
```

---

# 🔄 Update Ubuntu

```bash
apt update && apt upgrade -y
```

---

# 🛠 Install Python & Git

```bash
apt install python3 git -y
```

---

# 📂 Clone Projects From GitHub

```bash
git clone https://github.com/USERNAME/REPOSITORY.git
cd REPOSITORY
```

---

# ▶ Run Python File

```bash
python3 main.py
```

---

# ❌ Exit Linux

```bash
exit
```

